WEBVTT

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:15.610
-(GASPS)
-You're out!

00:00:17.210 --> 00:00:18.330
You're out.

00:00:19.570 --> 00:00:21.570
-(SIGHS)
-Hey, tough luck, Kris Kringle.

00:00:32.010 --> 00:00:34.050
-(CROWD CHEERING)
-(WHOOPING)

00:00:34.130 --> 00:00:35.330
Thank you.

00:00:36.170 --> 00:00:37.650
(CROWD CHEERING LOUDLY)

00:00:40.130 --> 00:00:41.170
Yeah!

00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:42.930
(WHOOPING) Yeah!

00:00:43.010 --> 00:00:44.090
We're down to two remaining teams,

00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:47.290
Roar Omega Roar and Oozma Kappa!

00:00:48.610 --> 00:00:51.450
Which leads us to the final event!

00:00:51.570 --> 00:00:54.450
"Every one of your skills
will be put to the test.

00:00:54.530 --> 00:00:57.850
"The Scare Simulator will prove
who's the best!"

00:00:58.050 --> 00:01:01.010
Tomorrow night you finally get to Scare

00:01:01.090 --> 00:01:02.170
in front of the whole school!

00:01:02.290 --> 00:01:04.850
Enjoy the attention while it lasts, boys.

00:01:05.530 --> 00:01:08.730
After you lose,
no one will remember you.

00:01:09.170 --> 00:01:13.010
Maybe. But when you lose,
no one will let you forget it.

00:01:14.090 --> 00:01:17.370
Oh, boy. That is a good point.

00:01:18.530 --> 00:01:19.970
Hey, Oozmas, you guys are awesome!

00:01:20.050 --> 00:01:22.010
You've got to teach us your moves.

00:01:22.090 --> 00:01:24.730
Well, then you're gonna
want to talk to this guy.

00:01:25.090 --> 00:01:27.090
Oh... (CHUCKLES)
Sure, I can teach you.

00:01:27.170 --> 00:01:28.730
All right. You want to hide
behind the chair?

00:01:28.810 --> 00:01:29.850
You have to become the chair.

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:32.770
MALE ANNOUNCER:
Thanks for coming, Dean.

00:01:34.410 --> 00:01:35.450
Dean Hardscrabble!

00:01:35.530 --> 00:01:38.130
If we get back into the Scaring program,

00:01:38.210 --> 00:01:39.530
I hope there's no hard feelings.

00:01:42.250 --> 00:01:44.770
Tomorrow, each of you must prove

00:01:44.850 --> 00:01:47.290
that you are undeniably scary.

00:01:48.890 --> 00:01:52.010
And I know for a fact
that one of you is not.

00:01:55.650 --> 00:01:56.730
(INDISTINCT)

00:01:57.530 --> 00:01:59.330
No. He works harder than anyone.

00:01:59.570 --> 00:02:00.730
Do you think he's scary?

00:02:00.930 --> 00:02:02.410
He's the heart and soul of the team!

00:02:02.730 --> 00:02:04.650
Do you think he's scary?

00:02:15.450 --> 00:02:16.410
(ROARS)

00:02:16.850 --> 00:02:19.210
We're going to win this thing
tomorrow, Sull, I can feel it!

00:02:19.850 --> 00:02:21.930
We'll finally have our lives back on track.

00:02:23.770 --> 00:02:25.010
Hey, Mike?

00:02:25.090 --> 00:02:28.290
You know, you've given me
a lot of really great tips.

00:02:28.370 --> 00:02:29.890
I'd love to return the favor sometime.

00:02:30.570 --> 00:02:32.610
Oh. Yeah, sure. Anytime.

00:02:32.690 --> 00:02:33.730
(SULLEY GRUNTS)

00:02:34.970 --> 00:02:36.170
-We're doing this now?
-Okay.

00:02:36.570 --> 00:02:37.970
You've memorized every textbook,

00:02:38.050 --> 00:02:39.970
every Scare Theory, and that is great.

00:02:40.050 --> 00:02:41.370
-Hey!
-(CAT YOWLS)

00:02:41.450 --> 00:02:43.210
But now it's time to forget all that.

00:02:43.290 --> 00:02:46.290
Just reach deep down
and let the scary out!

00:02:46.650 --> 00:02:48.210
Huh. Just feel it.

00:02:48.490 --> 00:02:49.770
Exactly. Go wild.

00:02:50.050 --> 00:02:52.210
I don't know. I've kind of
got my own technique.

00:02:52.650 --> 00:02:53.650
Give it a try.

00:02:55.730 --> 00:02:57.130
-(ROARS)
-Good, but bigger!

00:02:57.970 --> 00:02:59.370
-(ROARS)
-Nope. You're thinking again.

00:02:59.490 --> 00:03:01.210
-From the gut!
-(GRUNTING)

00:03:01.290 --> 00:03:02.610
Let the animal out!

00:03:03.090 --> 00:03:04.170
(ROARING)

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:05.890
Come on! Dig deep!

00:03:06.330 --> 00:03:07.370
(ROARING LOUDLY)

00:03:07.450 --> 00:03:10.050
SHERRIE: Boys! It's a school night!

00:03:12.330 --> 00:03:14.090
So, how was that?

00:03:15.450 --> 00:03:16.650
-Up top.
-Ha-ha!

00:03:17.650 --> 00:03:21.130
You know, it did feel different!
I feel like it's all coming together.

00:03:21.210 --> 00:03:24.130
Yup, this time tomorrow
the whole school is finally going to see

00:03:24.210 --> 00:03:26.050
what Mike Wazowski can do.

00:03:26.130 --> 00:03:27.690
(CHUCKLES) You're darn right.

00:03:34.690 --> 00:03:36.490
♪ Monsters University

00:03:36.610 --> 00:03:39.810
♪ We give our heart to you

00:03:39.890 --> 00:03:43.930
♪ Wherever children are dreaming

00:03:44.010 --> 00:03:46.450
♪ We'll bring them nightmares, too

00:03:47.210 --> 00:03:50.610
♪ Oh, Monsters University

00:03:50.690 --> 00:03:54.410
♪ Alma Mater hail to you ♪

00:03:54.490 --> 00:03:57.130
FEMALE ANNOUNCER:
Welcome to the final competition

00:03:57.210 --> 00:03:58.530
of the Scare Games.

00:03:58.970 --> 00:04:01.050
-(CROWD CHEERING)
-(MARCHING BAND PLAYING)

00:04:01.610 --> 00:04:04.050
Whoo! Yeah! All right!

00:04:05.530 --> 00:04:07.930
MALE ANNOUNCER:
It's time to see how terrifying

00:04:08.050 --> 00:04:09.450
you really are,

00:04:09.810 --> 00:04:11.570
in the Scare Simulators!

00:04:12.450 --> 00:04:14.210
FEMALE ANNOUNCER: But be warned.

00:04:14.330 --> 00:04:16.250
Each simulated Scare has been set

00:04:16.330 --> 00:04:19.090
to the highest difficulty level.

00:04:19.170 --> 00:04:20.130
The highest level?

00:04:20.210 --> 00:04:22.890
FEMALE ANNOUNCER:
First Scarers to the starting line.

00:04:22.970 --> 00:04:25.570
Okay, just like we planned.
I'll go first. Then, Don...

00:04:25.650 --> 00:04:27.690
Hold on. Mike's the one
who started all this

00:04:28.250 --> 00:04:30.890
and I think it's only right
if he's the one who finishes it.

00:04:31.530 --> 00:04:32.770
I think you should go last.

00:04:33.130 --> 00:04:34.210
ALL: Yes!

00:04:34.290 --> 00:04:35.330
Yeah, Mike. Finish strong!

00:04:36.450 --> 00:04:39.170
All right. Don, you okay going first?

00:04:39.250 --> 00:04:41.410
I guess I'm as ready as I'll ever be.

00:04:42.050 --> 00:04:43.970
ALL: Oozma Kappa!

00:04:44.210 --> 00:04:45.730
-(CROWD CHEERING)
-MONSTER: Go Oozmas!

00:04:45.850 --> 00:04:47.530
I'm gonna do it.
I'm going to beat this guy.

00:04:47.650 --> 00:04:50.730
Hey, Bruiser!
You take it easy on grandpa.

00:04:50.810 --> 00:04:54.170
-(LAUGHS EVILLY)
-Unleash the beast, Don!

00:04:54.850 --> 00:04:56.210
Okay, then.

00:04:57.050 --> 00:04:59.330
(BUZZER SOUNDING)

00:05:03.050 --> 00:05:04.290
(PANTING)

00:05:08.890 --> 00:05:09.930
(CROWD GASPING)

00:05:23.010 --> 00:05:24.090
(GASPS)

00:05:24.690 --> 00:05:25.770
(SQUEAKING)

00:05:26.810 --> 00:05:28.010
-(ROARS)
-(SCREAMING)

00:05:30.490 --> 00:05:31.490
(GRUNTS)

00:05:32.890 --> 00:05:33.930
(ROARING)

00:05:38.330 --> 00:05:39.930
-(ROARING)
-(SCREAMING)

00:05:41.010 --> 00:05:42.090
(DINGS)

00:05:42.290 --> 00:05:43.290
(ALL CHEERING)

00:05:43.810 --> 00:05:44.970
Huh? Huh?

00:05:46.570 --> 00:05:48.810
Thanks for taking it easy on grandpa.

00:05:49.090 --> 00:05:50.570
(ALL GASPING)

00:05:54.850 --> 00:05:56.690
FEMALE ANNOUNCER:
Next group to the starting line.

00:05:57.770 --> 00:05:58.970
BOTH: Let's do this.

00:06:05.010 --> 00:06:06.010
(ROARS)

00:06:06.330 --> 00:06:07.330
(DINGS)

00:06:07.450 --> 00:06:09.010
-(CHEERING)
-Yes! Yeah!

00:06:12.330 --> 00:06:14.010
-(BOTH ROARING)
-(SCREAMING)

00:06:14.250 --> 00:06:15.250
(DINGS)

00:06:15.530 --> 00:06:16.530
(CHEERING)

00:06:22.970 --> 00:06:23.970
(SCREAMING)

00:06:24.330 --> 00:06:25.330
(DINGS)

00:06:25.610 --> 00:06:27.450
(CHEERING ENTHUSIASTICALLY)

00:06:28.570 --> 00:06:29.690
-(ROARS)
-(SCREAMS)

00:06:31.690 --> 00:06:32.850
-Come on, Art.
-Come on, buddy.

00:06:32.930 --> 00:06:34.090
-You can do it.
-(ALL ENCOURAGING)

00:06:44.010 --> 00:06:45.170
-(SCREAMING)
-(DINGS)

00:06:45.610 --> 00:06:47.050
-Yes!
-(CHEERING)

00:06:47.250 --> 00:06:48.370
-(ROARS)
-(SCREAMS)

00:06:48.690 --> 00:06:49.690
CROWD: Aw!

00:06:49.850 --> 00:06:51.090
(ALL GROANING)

00:06:52.730 --> 00:06:56.250
MALE ANNOUNCER:
Next up, Sullivan and Boggs!

00:06:57.730 --> 00:06:58.770
(BUZZER SOUNDS)

00:07:07.210 --> 00:07:08.410
You got this, Sull.

